  "scientificConclusion": "V78 found that pregame route-aware warnings retrospectively captured 47 of 138 losses, but also flagged 39 original wins. Counter-side flipping those cases improved the same historical sample from 254-138-3 to 262-130-3, yet failed season robustness because 2025 worsened. Vetoing the 86 warning cases produced a much higher retained-sample hit rate of 70.26% with 78.23% pick-day coverage and approximately 69-71% hit rate in each season, but this remains adaptive same-sample evidence motivated by V77 and cannot be promoted live without fresh validation. The evidence currently supports prospective validation of a warning/no-play architecture more strongly than automatic counter-side reversal.",
